  "title": "Champagne Fairs",
  "summary": "Cyclical international trade fairs in the Champagne region of France, held in four towns (Troyes, Provins, Lagny, Bar-sur-Aube) under the Counts of Champagne, who set the calendar, protected merchants and taxed goods. The BnF says they dominated European trade in the 12th and 13th centuries; they declined in the early 14th.",
